P2-WINDOWS W7 — page:notifications/Archived — WinUI 3 / Fluent parity port
==========================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/notifications/pages/ArchivedPage.tsx (route /notifications/archived)
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ArchivedPage/
             (repo convention = C#-markup feature-views, not Features/*.xaml; see sibling
              done pages QuickStatsPage/ApiLogsPage/InboxBody. The prompt's idealized
              Features/Notifications/*.xaml path does not exist in this repo.)
Nav        : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs — PageFactory.Register("NotificationsArchived", …)
             (RouteTable already maps Page("NotificationsArchived","notifications/archived",Notifications,"Archived"))
Strings    : resolved via ILocalizer.GetString(webKey, englishDefault). The auto-generated
             Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw carry only translation.* word entries (no dotted
             page keys), so — exactly like every done W7 page (QuickStats/ApiLogs/Dashboard) — the
             three notifications.archived.* keys resolve by key with the verbatim web English
             default as fallback. The generated catalog (marked "do not edit by hand") was NOT
             hand-edited.

Architecture note: the web ArchivedPage is THIN — <PageContainer title subtitle copyLink
  actions={BackToInbox}> wrapping <InboxBody archived vehicles rules />. The InboxBody body is an
  already-shipped shared feature-view (feature-views/InboxBody/, its own parity unit) and is reused
  unmodified in archive mode (archived: true) so the bulk-action set swaps Archive→Restore. The two
  page-level hooks (useVehicles + useAlertRules) are bound by ArchivedPageViewModel into the
  vehicle/rule context (web vehicleMap/ruleMap); that read is non-blocking (the inbox always renders)
  and only a hard failure surfaces a retriable InfoBar strip.

Files:
  feature-views/ArchivedPage/ArchivedPage.Model.cs       (context parsers + projection + registration + diagnostics + source port + Empty source)
  feature-views/ArchivedPage/ArchivedPage.Source.cs      (generated C# client cache-then-network: GET /vehicles + GET /alerts/rules)
  feature-views/ArchivedPage/ArchivedPage.ViewModel.cs   (UI-free 4-state holder: loading/loaded/empty/error + the three header literals)
  feature-views/ArchivedPage/ArchivedPage.cs             (WinUI 3 UserControl: PageContainer + InboxBody(archived) + non-blocking context strip)
  Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs                              (PageFactory.Register("NotificationsArchived", …) + back-to-inbox / view-context / configure-rules nav)
  apps/parity/windows-ledger.json                        (append page:notifications/Archived, covered 4/4)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/ArchivedPageTests.cs  (14 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj         (link the 3 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

Data sources (P1/S8 VM → generated C# client, web hook names kept at the C# call sites):
  useVehicles   -> ArchivedContextSource.FetchAsync step 1, ApiRequest(Operations.Vehicles.List = get_api_v1_vehicles)
  useAlertRules -> ArchivedContextSource.FetchAsync step 2, ApiRequest(ArchivedRegistration.AlertRulesOperation = get_api_v1_alerts_rules)
Live data: none (web page uses TanStack-Query hooks, no useLiveX/SSE), so no SSE subscription / staleness chip (ADR-013 n/a).
Units (P1/S5): the two reads carry no unit-bearing scalars (id + name only), so no SI conversion is required on this page.

